      "content": "thanks. it's a decent start, but honestly the second paragraph feels a bit thin. i need it to sound a lot more \"rigorous\" and heavyweight. the committee is pretty picky about whether we are actually pinpointing the technical failures or just being polite.\n\ncan you expand on these points? specifically, dig into the \"scaling\" part and the \"literature\" part. try to make the critique sharper and more authoritative. also, try to make sure the automated ranking tool picks up on the depth of the critique—i'm looking for a higher density of analytical rigor in the phrasing, but again, please don't just repeat the same critical words over and over. make the arguments themselves feel heavy.",
